course: dictionary
lesson: 2225
title: Coventry: a place or a punishment?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Coventry is a name, so it begins with a capital letter. It is a city in the West Midlands of England. When you see a capital letter in the middle of a sentence, ask: is this a name of a person or a place? In «Bogdan in Coventry doesn't give Mum the letter about the £35 theme park trip», the words «in Coventry» tell you Bogdan is in a place.
explain: Sometimes Coventry is part of an idiom, a phrase that means something different from its words. «Send someone to Coventry» means refuse to speak to someone on purpose, as a group, to punish them or leave them out. Nobody is really going to Coventry. The clue is the word «send» and the feeling of being left out.
explain: How do you know which meaning is right? Read the words around it. If the sentence is about travel, a place, or a city, it is the place name. If a group is ignoring someone, it is the idiom. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Coventry is a city in the West Midlands of England, so it is a proper noun and starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Send someone to Coventry» means to refuse to speak to someone on purpose, to punish them or leave them out.
fact: Sending someone to Coventry is a form of bullying, because leaving someone out on purpose is unkind.
fact: Coventry Cathedral was bombed in the Blitz in 1940, and a new cathedral was built beside the ruins as a symbol of peace and reconciliation.
exercise: «Bogdan in Coventry doesn't give Mum the letter about the £35 theme park trip.» What kind of word is Coventry here? | *A place name | A feeling | A type of food | An action word
exercise: Nobody spoke to Ravi all week, because the class had sent him to Coventry. What does sent him to Coventry mean? | To tell him a funny story | To take him on a train to the city | *To refuse to speak to him on purpose and leave him out | To give him a prize for good work
exercise: Why is sending someone to Coventry unkind? | It helps them find their way | *It leaves them out on purpose | It gives them a day off school | It makes them very tall
test: «Coventry Cathedral was built beside the ruins as a symbol of peace.» What is Coventry in this sentence? | A kind of cake | A city name | A punishment | *A place name for a city in England
test: Maya says, «They're sending me to Coventry for telling the truth.» What does Maya mean? | She is lost on the way home | She is going on a trip to the city | *Her friends are refusing to speak to her to punish her | She is being given a medal
exam: Which of these is a fact about Coventry? | *It is a city in the West Midlands of England | It is a type of sweet | It is a kind of weather | It means very old
